 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-idm19803040\" class=\"interactive\" data-label=\"\">\n<h3 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h3>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<h4 data-type=\"title\" id=\"7\" class=\"os-subtitle\">\n  <span class=\"os-subtitle-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h4>\n        <span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idm47881280\" data-alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\">\n        <img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20220509.174553/resources/d69bbdfa8920ec655a25c6f2919e803835d81e75\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\" width=\"120\" id=\"8\">\n    </span>\n<p id=\"fs-idm1483088\">Click through this <a href=\"https://openstaxcollege.org/l/bird_evolution\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">interactive site</a> to see how island birds evolved in evolutionary increments from 5 million years ago to today.</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 639830,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Name three examples of adaptive radiation, and provide a brief statement about each one.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246838,
     "content_html": "Domestic dogs – There are over 300 distinct dog breeds. Cows – There are over 800 cow breeds recognized worldwide. Domestic cats – Cats have changed drastically in just a few thousand years."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246837,
     "content_html": "Whales and fish – Although it has been roughly 400 million years since fish and mammals diverged, whales and fish are morphologically similar. Birds and butterflies – Although the common ancestor between vertebrates and insects lived even longer ago than the common ancestor between whales and fish, birds and butterflies both developed flight. Rabbits and kangaroos – Although it has been over 150 million years since their divergence, rabbits and kangaroos both developed powerful jumping legs."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246839,
     "content_html": "Hawaiian silverswords-There are about 30 species evolved from one parent species. Madagascar lemurs-Their common ancestor likely arrived to Madagascar over 60 million years ago. Hawaiian fruit fly-There are 500 species of fruit fly from one parent species."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246836,
     "content_html": "Beetles – There are about 350,000 species of beetles that we know of. Birds – There are almost 10,000 species of birds in existence. Frogs – There are almost 5,000 species of frogs worldwide."
    }
   ],
